# vlib.bundle (vlib.sh) tags v0.1.0, written for mach 6 with `mach = "^6"` and a profile key mach 7
# removed, and v0.2.0, written for mach 7. no command holds v0.1.0's manifest to this schema: its
# compiler range refuses it first, or a selection that has moved past it does
# app selects vlib at tag/v0.1.0, so each walker names the range
1 dep pull app | app -> vlib requires mach ^6
1 dep pull app |! is not allowed
1 build app | app -> vlib requires mach ^6
1 dep verify app | app -> vlib requires mach ^6
# app2 holds vlib at v0.1.0 while liba, its path dependency, selects tag/v0.2.0
1 dep add app2 vlib --git ../vlib.bundle --ref tag/v0.1.0 | app2 -> vlib requires mach ^6
1 dep pull app2 | run `mach dep update <path> vlib`
1 dep verify app2 | run `mach dep update <path> vlib`
# a build reads no selector, so it names the range
1 build app2 | app2 -> liba -> vlib requires mach ^6
0 dep update app2 vlib | updated  vlib
0 build app2 | built  app2
0 dep verify app2 | verified  app2
# resolution reads a release's range before its schema
1 dep add app3 vlib --git ../vlib.bundle --range ^0.1 | vlib 0.1.0 requires mach ^6
0 dep add app3 vlib --git ../vlib.bundle --range ^0.2 | added  [dep.vlib]
